  "summary": "Three preprints posted 17 to 20 November 2026 apply deep-learning and diffusion models to editing outcome prediction.",
  "synthesis": "The shared thread is predicting DNA editing outcomes from local sequence context. A Cas9 study analysing about 37,000 sites examines single-nucleotide microhomology in precision editing, reports that A-rich PAM editors are predicted better, and introduces the CRIfuser diffusion model. A second preprint presents 2CaP-5, a deep-learning model that predicts LbCas12a crRNA editing efficiency in wheat protoplasts from about 1,000 tested guides, and that can be retrained with 500 crRNAs. BEguided offers variant-specific guide design and comparison across 38 base-editor profiles, with BEguidedOFF for off-target prediction. What is new is the use of diffusion and deep-learning architectures, and of systematic cross-editor evaluation, for these tasks. All three are preprints, and the summaries do not report head-to-head benchmarks against established tools.",
